                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 3 at 2:51PM MST until November 3 at 9:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Havasu Creek basin in...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\n\n* Until 900 PM MST Tuesday.\n\n* At 251 PM MST, A river gauge on Cataract Creek below Heather Wash\nreported a rapid rise of 2.7 feet. This rise is due to runoff from\nheavy rain that occurred on previous days. Flash flooding is\nalready occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Runoff from the most recent storm is producing flash\nflooding in and around the Havasu Creek basin.\n\nSOURCE...River gauge reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of areas in and around the Havasu Creek\nbasin.\n\n* For Cataract Creek at Cataract Creek Below Heather Wash:\nAt 1:30pm the stage was 6.4 feet.\nFlood Stage is 7.5 feet.\nImpacts:\nAt 7.5 feet: 450 cfs flow. May cause minor flooding downstream in\nSupai campground 4 to 7 hours later.\nAt 10.0 feet: 1520 cfs flow. May cause moderate flooding downstream\nin Suapi villago 4 to 7 hours later.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nSupai, Havasupai Reservation, Little Navajo Falls, Mooney Falls and\nBeaver Falls.\n\nThis includes the Colorado River between river miles 157 and 158.\n\nThis includes the following swimming holes...\nAll swimming holes on Havasu Creek near Supai.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nColorado River, Havasu Creek, Sinyella Canyon and Little Coyote\nCanyon.",
                "instruction": "Campers and hikers should hustle to higher ground immediately! Stay\naway from creeks and washes!\n\nFoot bridges will be washed out in Supai Campground. Some campsites\nwill be flooded. Campers may be stranded in portions of the\ncampground.",
                "response": "Avoid",
